hi I'm Matt Welch for reason TV I'm here  in Tampa at the republican national  convention we're here on day 1 on radio  row where 15,000 journalists are trying  to figure out if there's any stories to  cover we think there's three worth  watching this week story number one  what's going to happen the Ron Paul  movement within the Republican Party and  is it likely to stay there and is it  likely to vote Republican there is a  Paul festival over the weekend where the  man who got upwards of eleven percent of  the vote in the primary season give a  rip roarin speech against blowback and  against the foreign policy of the  Republican Party in fact how the  Republican Party deals with this rump  faction is going to be a source of much  conflict and has been already story  number two will the real Paul Ryan be  allowed to stand up whether or not he  can the vice presidential pick is  supposed to leave one of the great wonks  of Washington and a man who's finally  serious enough to talk about and tackle  entitlement reform which this country so  desperately needs yet the presidential  nominee mitt romney has proven to be  decidedly not very serious or wonky when  it comes to things like cutting and  reforming Medicare so is this not to  fiscal conservatism as good as it is  likely to get the story will be  following here finally story number  three what's going to happen to social  conservatives and the whole idea that  the government should leave us the hell  alone not just an economic matters but  in personal matters the week before the  convention big hubbub about various  comments about abortion and rape and now  this week there's going to be a lot of  discussion about immigration  highlighting the fact perhaps that  Romney is no george w bush when it comes  to treating people who came here to  better their lives but broke American  law while doing it seeing how these  stories play out the background of 2012  is going to tell us a lot about whether  Mitt Romney and Paul Ryan are going to  win but more importantly whether the  Republican Party is going to get serious  at long last about embracing freedom for  reason TV I am Matt Welch
 

